  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 249 AM EST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nPleasant and dry weather continues through the middle of the week \nwith high pressure parked over the region. Temperatures will warm up \nslightly, but remain around normal with highs in the 70s, and \novernight lows in the upper 30s to low 40s. Confidence in the \ndetails of the forecast start to drop off for the second half of the \nweek, but there is great model agreement on the overall pattern with \na strong trough dropping over the Eastern US. This system will \nlikely support at least slight rain chances for portions of North GA \nThursday into Friday, before the associated cold front moves through \nand brings in a cool and dry airmass for next weekend. It is looking \nincreasingly likely that this will be the coolest airmass of the \nseason thus far, with lows at or below freezing across much of the \narea, and high temperatures topping out in the 50s to low 60s.",
